course: dictionary
lesson: 5577
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The same word can mean different things in different places. Context tells you which meaning is right. Read this: «In western Ukraine the Principality of Galicia-Volhynia was strong in the 13th century; Prince Danylo of Halych received a royal crown from a papal envoy (a messenger of the Pope) in 1253, and Lviv was named after his son Lev, though Danylo still had to accept the Mongols as his overlords (masters).»
explain: In that sentence, Lev is a person's name. The clues are «named after his son», which tells you a son was called Lev. A name is a word for a person, so you know Lev here is not money or an animal.
explain: Lev can also be money. A Bulgarian lev is the money of Bulgaria, and one lev is divided into 100 stotinki. In Russian and Ukrainian, «лев» means lion, but that is a different language, so do not expect it in an English sentence. When you meet lev, look at the words around it: numbers and prices mean money, and «son» or «named after» means a name.
fact: A lev is the money of Bulgaria.
fact: One lev is divided into 100 stotinki.
fact: The plural of lev is leva, for more than one lev.
fact: Lev is a man's first name, and it means «heart» in Hebrew.
fact: In Russian and Ukrainian, «лев» means lion. Lev is not an English word.
exercise: A Bulgarian coin is called a lev. How many stotinki make one lev? | *100 | 10 | 50 | 1000
exercise: «Lviv was named after his son Lev.» In this sentence, what is Lev? | The word for lion | A river in Ukraine | *A person's first name | A king's crown
exercise: In Russian, «лев» means what? | *Lion | A river | Money | A royal crown
test: The plural of lev, when you mean more than one Bulgarian lev, is: | levas | levi | levs | *leva
test: In a story, Lev is a boy's name. Which clue shows that? | It is next to the word stotinki | It is a river in Bulgaria | *It is a first name, like Lev Tolstoy | It is the price of bread
exam: Ella reads «The lev is worth 100 stotinki» in a maths problem. What does lev mean here? | *Bulgarian money | A Hebrew word for heart | A lion | A man's first name
